# ADR Reporting and Documentation

## 1. Objective
To prepare a structured Adverse Drug Reaction (ADR) reporting form using a simulated patient case scenario, following the basic principles of pharmacovigilance documentation.

## 2. Introduction
Adverse Drug Reaction reporting is an essential component of pharmacovigilance. It involves collecting, documenting and evaluating information related to suspected adverse reactions associated with medicinal products.

Proper ADR documentation helps healthcare professionals identify potential drug-related risks and improve medication safety.

