## 9. Additional Clinical Information

The patient developed multiple symptoms following the initiation of amoxicillin therapy. Information regarding drug withdrawal, rechallenge, previous allergy history, laboratory investigations and alternative causes is unavailable.

Further clinical evaluation is required.

## 10. Documentation and Reporting Process

1. Collect patient demographic information.
2. Record all suspected and concomitant medications.
3. Document the adverse reaction and onset timeline.
4. Assess the suspected relationship between medicine and reaction.
5. Record seriousness and clinical outcome when available.
6. Collect reporter and healthcare institution details.
7. Submit a complete report through the appropriate pharmacovigilance reporting channel.

## 11. Conclusion

This simulated case demonstrates the importance of structured ADR reporting and documentation. Amoxicillin was identified as the leading suspected medicine based on the available clinical timeline. Accurate documentation of patient information, suspected medicines, reaction details and reporter information is essential for effective pharmacovigilance and patient safety.

